87-Kim1"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Yeo</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name><name><surname>Jang</surname><given-names>HC</given-names></name><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>WB</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Clinical responses to smallpox vaccine in vaccinia-naive and previously vaccinated populations: undiluted and diluted Lancy-Vaxina vaccine in a single-blind, randomized, prospective trial.</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source><volume>192</volume><fpage>1066</fpage><lpage>70</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16107961</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004087-Orr1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Orr</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Forman</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Marcus</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Lustig</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Paran</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Clinical and immune responses after revaccination of israeli adults with the Lister strain of vaccinia virus.</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source><volume>190</volume><fpage>1295</fpage><lpage>302</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15346341</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004087-Combadiere1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Combadiere</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Boissonnas</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Carcelain</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Lefranc</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Samri</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Distinct time effects of vaccination on long-term proliferative and IFN-gamma-producing T cell memory to smallpox in humans.</article-title><source>J Exp Med</source><volume>199</volume><fpage>1585</fpage><lpage>93</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15184506</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004087-Frey1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Frey</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Newman</surname><given-names>FK</given-names></name><name><surname>Yan</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Lottenbach</surname><given-names>KR</given-names></name><name><surname>Belshe</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Response to smallpox vaccine in persons immunized in the distant past.</article-title><source>JAMA</source><volume>289</volume><fpage>3295</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12824212</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004087-Hammarlund1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hammarlund</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Lewis</surname><given-names>MW</given-names></name><name><surname>Carter</surname><given-names>SV</given-names></name><name><surname>Amanna</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Hansen</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Multiple diagnostic techniques identify previously vaccinated individuals with protective immunity against monkeypox.</article-title><source>Nat Med</source><volume>11</volume><fpage>1005</fpage><lpage>11</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16086024</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004087-Ennis1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ennis</surname><given-names>FA</given-names></name><name><surname>Cruz</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Demkowicz</surname><given-names>WE</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name><name><surname>Rothman</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>McClain</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Primary induction of human CD8&#x0002b; cytotoxic T lymphocytes and interferon-gamma-producing T cells after smallpox vaccination.</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source><volume>185</volume><fpage>1657</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12023773</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004087-Demkowicz1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Demkowicz</surname><given-names>WE</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name><name><surname>Littaua</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Ennis</surname><given-names>FA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Human cytotoxic T-cell memory: long-lived responses to vaccinia virus.</article-title><source>J Virol</source><volume>70</volume><fpage>2627</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8642697</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004087-Kim2"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Yeo</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>KH</given-names></name><name><surname>Bang</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>HB</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>The persistence of humoral and cellular immunities more than three decades after smallpo